  "verbalization": "The compound [(1S,4aS,6S,8aS)-4,8a-dimethyl-6-[(2R)-6-methyl-4-oxohept-5-en-2-yl]-2-oxo-1,4a,5,6,7,8-hexahydronaphthalen-1-yl] acetate is implicated in the interaction with SMMC-7721 through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target for HCC1599, which in turn is targeted by Polyporenic Acid B and SB-269970, both of which directly interact with SMMC-7721. Additionally, the compound is associated with CD70 antigen, which is targeted by Isohalitulin and SB-269970, further linking the compound to SMMC-7721. The evidence suggests that the compound may exert its effects through mechanisms involving the CD70 antigen pathway, potentially modulating immune responses or signaling pathways in the cancer cell. The integration of these targets and their interactions implies a possible role in targeting SMMC-7721 through multiple molecular mechanisms, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
